{%- comment -%}
    The payment icons that show in your theme are determined by your store’s payment settings and the customer’s region and currency. 
    If you want to add or remove payment icons without changing your payment settings, then you can do so by editing your theme code.

    Learn more: https://docs.openthinking.net/themes/bullet/kb/payment-icons/

    /!\ Changing this file will have an impact on all payment icons on the site.

    Custom: the card badges were replaced with the UPI and Cash on Delivery
    marks (uploaded in Content > Files). Sizing is handled in
    custom-footer.css, because the 29x19 box custom.css gives .payment-icon
    would squash these logos.
    To revert to Shopify's automatic icons, delete the <img> lines below and restore:
    for type in shop.enabled_payment_types
        echo type | payment_type_svg_tag: class: 'payment-icon'
    endfor
{%- endcomment -%}

<img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0774/6987/6271/files/UPI-Logo.png?v=1785928386" alt="UPI" class="payment-icon payment-icon--upi" height="22" loading="lazy">
<img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0774/6987/6271/files/cod_icon_e27ecc82-e5f6-4122-aadf-5f9eaaa958d7.png?v=1785929489" alt="Cash on delivery" class="payment-icon payment-icon--upi" height="22" loading="lazy">
